finding={'id':'Q448','title':'Copied partial cyclic strict-workload checks admit a vector starting at the stage length','source':S+'sync_partial_cyclic.rs:validate_with_config,SyncPartialCyclicJob::execute_task;'+S+'async_partial_cyclic.rs:validate_with_config,AsyncPartialCyclicJob::execute_task','evidence':'Both partial cyclic validators compute the last unit/task vector start and reject only max_position > num_stage_elements. A start exactly at the element count is already outside the stage. For63 vectors of4 elements with32 loading units, each unit receives2 tasks; final start252 equals a252-element stage and both exact validator bodies admit it. Strict execution takes the copy/store branch unconditionally despite balanced_workload=false. The full cyclic validators use divisibility and reject the same imbalance. Balanced64-vector controls pass;62-vector further-overrun controls reject. The sync/async copies share the defect rather than one delegating to a common scheduling check.','status':'documented, not repaired; exact host predicate witness with explicit dependency stubs','scope':'Eight numeric cases in a10-case CPU probe compile exact sync/async partial/full validator bodies. Shape/count/type methods are explicit scalar doubles; remaining tiling/swizzle/device capability validators deliberately return Ok. Proves the named predicate defect, not complete blueprint/routine acceptance of a concrete tile, current selected caller reachability, CubeDSL lowering, GPU corruption or a particular physical bounds-failure mode. The other2 cases inspect ordered-loader flow admission only.','repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented in read-only full-source audit','reason':'Share one strict-workload schedule predicate, preferably balanced vector-count divisibility or explicit half-open byte/vector extent checking. Apply the same model to full/partial and sync/async readers; retain relaxed guards and preserve per-stage versus total-buffer extent distinction. Qualify a real blueprint before asserting a current device incident.'},'verification':NAME,'diagnostics':[probe_name]}
