rows=[
 ('Full and partial reader wrappers share vocabulary but repeat job lifetime logic','FullStageGlobalReader and PartialStageGlobalReader both own global iterator, stage memory, runtime config and optional precomputed jobs.',
  [R+'reader/full_reader.rs',R+'reader/partial_reader.rs',R+'reader/shared.rs'],
  'Both implement nearly identical JobExecutor/task-counter loops; partial adds A/B job pairs and stage selection. Precomputed job clones are re-created per view load while RuntimeCell iterator offset is shared. StageFamily controls create/free and buffer-index views. This is real duplicated wrapper implementation around a common trait, with algorithm-specific buffer ownership rather than two mathematical authorities.'),
 ('Unused cooperative clear policy is a dead contract surface','FullLoadingStrategy declares SHOULD_CLEAR=false and AsyncFullCooperativeLoading overrides it true.',
  [R+'reader/full_reader.rs',S+'async_full_cooperative.rs'],
  'Whole-crate identifier search finds only the declaration and override, with no consumer. Full reader creation/load does not clear based on it. Cooperative loading copies possibly shortened windows to full destinations, so padding/initialization semantics still need backend API proof. The unused flag is confirmed cruft; stale-data numerical failure is not demonstrated and may depend on copy intrinsic semantics.'),
 ('Reader layout bounds deliberately delegate to lower views','FullStageLayout and TiledLayout map logical positions while always reporting in bounds.',
  [R+'layout/stage.rs',R+'layout/tiled.rs',R+'layout/mod.rs',R+'mod.rs'],
  'FullStageLayout maps row/column positions from physical stage layout; TiledLayout expands lhs/rhs stage count along different K axes. Their safety depends on underlying GlobalLayout checked predicates and per-reader task bounds, so read_checked at this layer is not an independent stage-capacity check. Q448 shows the separate scheduler admission defect. No actual layered-view bounds execution was run.'),
 ('Async copy width and transfer visibility have explicit shared primitives','async_copy_from uses a128-bit transfer width, computes checked source length and applies stage swizzle.',
  [S+'async_copy.rs',S+'async_barrier.rs',S+'async_tma.rs',S+'sync.rs'],
  'AsyncBarrier waits at a shared barrier; AsyncCopy commits copy operations before waiting; TMA arrival expects combined lhs/rhs bytes and waits on a token. Synchronous uses sync_cube. These mechanisms are intentionally different completion authorities; task issuance or Result from host validation is not transfer visibility. Alignment and numeric conversion semantics require the earlier validators and external intrinsic contract.'),
 ('Full and partial cyclic readers have separate copies of workload arithmetic','Sync/async full cyclic variants use strict divisibility; partial variants use a duplicated maximum-start formula.',
  [S+'sync_full_cyclic.rs',S+'async_full_cyclic.rs',S+'sync_partial_cyclic.rs',S+'async_partial_cyclic.rs'],
  'Q448 records the shared off-by-one in the two partial implementations. All variants build similar unit base/jump/task count and strict-versus-relaxed branches, then map tiles and stage offsets independently. Partial copies additionally offset lhs columns or rhs rows by buffer index. One scheduling model could remove multiple independently maintained admission checks; the concrete supported tile constraints still need later routine qualification.'),
 ('Strided and tilewise loaders add distinct distribution constraints','Strided loaders distribute linear stage vectors; tilewise loaders assign whole tiles per plane.',
  [S+'sync_full_strided.rs',S+'async_full_strided.rs',S+'async_partial_strided.rs',S+'sync_full_tilewise.rs',S+'sync_partial_tilewise.rs'],
  'They repeat divisibility/task sizing, global-to-stage layout and swizzle calculations. Tilewise requires tile count divisible by loader plane count and vectors per plane divisible by plane width; partial restricts lhs RowMajor and rhs ColMajor tiling order. Async paths require128-bit copy slices. These are shared algorithm families with separate code paths, not proof every combination is valid.'),
 ('Ordered reader validates shape distribution but not specialized-LHS flow itself','SyncFullOrderedLoading layers lhs-only, rows-per-plane and vector-distribution checks over tilewise jobs.',
  [S+'sync_full_ordered.rs',G+'multi_stage/ordered/matmul.rs',G+'multi_stage/ordered/setup.rs'],
  'Its exact validator accepts MainOnly and LoadOnly configs with the same numeric dimensions in2 CPU cases, with other tiling validation stubbed. Ordered kernel separately refuses specialized lhs. The host loader validator has no corresponding input_load_flow check; higher-level routine admission remains unread, so this is a late-validation followup rather than a confirmed current host-success bug. It reuses actual SyncFullTilewiseJob, a real shared execution implementation.'),
 ('TMA broadcast restrictions are explicitly admitted before descriptor loads','validate_tma_with_problem rejects mixed broadcast/nonbroadcast batches unless one operand has total batch count1.',
  [S+'base.rs',S+'async_full_tma.rs',S+'async_partial_tma.rs'],
  'This resolves the earlier concern about unsupported partial batch broadcasting being unguarded in this path, provided callers run validate_with_problem. Quantized inputs are explicitly refused and strides require16-byte alignment. Full/partial TMA task builders are separate and mirror swizzle task-count logic; tensor-map hardware owns out-of-bounds fill, not the generic GlobalLayout checks. No actual TMA descriptor/device run.'),
 ('Problem validation and config validation are separate required admissions','LoadingValidation exposes both validate_with_problem and validate_with_config.',
  [S+'base.rs',S+'async_full_cooperative.rs',S+'async_full_cyclic.rs',S+'async_partial_cyclic.rs'],
  'Async copy/TMA config checks compare dtype size, not exact numeric type identity, despite error strings saying types must be the same. Problem checks disallow quantization and require aligned strides; Acc/Out enter unreachable branches in async-copy/TMA problem helpers. AL accumulator validation is omitted by several family callers, so generic accumulator-loader compatibility needs later trace. Same-size byte transfer semantics may be intentional reinterpretation; no numeric conversion defect proved.'),
 ('Plane role ownership is re-exported from one root vocabulary','Specialization roles.rs forwards root PlaneFlowConfig/Counts/Partition/Rule rather than redefining them.',
  [G+'specialization/roles.rs',G+'specialization/config.rs',G+'specialization/specializer.rs',G+'specialization/mod.rs'],
  'LoadFlows computes reader plane divisors and chooses LoadOnlyFirst; Specializer carries whether each flow loads lhs/rhs. Local config code owns the policy, root types own identity. best_divisor_close_to_reference starts at1 even for0, so direct MainOnly/MainOnly with Some(reader_tasks) could create an idle load-only plane; normal callers condition the Some on specialization. Root role math remains unread next area, no concrete wasted-work claim.'),
 ('Writer shared-memory clamp matches the budget calculation','PartitionedStage::new forces tiles_per_partition row/col to1 before actual shared stage allocation.',
  [G+'write/stage.rs',M+'components/batch/partitioned_matmul/setup.rs'],
  'This verifies the clamp assumed by out_smem_bytes in the earlier budget code. Plane/Unit writers stage one tile per owning primitive and reuse it across output tile events. Input stage free occurs after barriers; SimpleMatmul notes output stage was declared earlier and therefore does not automatically reuse those freed bytes. No live compiler allocation-size or physical-memory receipt, but the source-level accounting ownership now agrees.'),
 ('Plane and unit writers expose different completion protocols','Plane writer synchronizes within the plane before/after staged reads; unit writer serially emits its owned vectors.',
  [G+'write/plane.rs',G+'write/unit.rs',G+'write/base.rs',G+'write/event.rs',G+'write/mod.rs'],
  'PlaneWriter validates output vector width divides the tile contiguous width; UnitWriter uses default no-op config validation and floor-divides vectors per tile. Stage/tile admission may guarantee its divisibility later. WriteEvent TileStored invokes actual writes; events are re-exported from generic tile vocabulary. Existing writer tests fully read, not run. Vector gather mismatch branches require a separate caller contract; default stage builder uses matching stage/global output widths.'),
 ('Single-stage path validates no specialization and uses accumulator loader sync separately','SimpleMatmulFamily rejects specialized load flows and sets MainOnly for all readers.',
  [G+'single_stage/simple/setup.rs',G+'single_stage/simple/matmul.rs',G+'single_stage/simple/mod.rs',G+'single_stage/mod.rs'],
  'Its optional accumulator has AL-specific barrier creation and sync, unlike some multi-stage reuse patterns. K0 produces zero iterations here rather than the double-buffer subtraction; output initialization still depends on accumulator initialization/Tile loading. Lhs/rhs config validation and writer validation happen host-side, AL remains unvalidated by these methods. No actual zero-K or accumulator numerical run.'),
 ('Stage enums are shared payload owners with substantive common construction','StageMatmul carries one PartitionedStageMatmul data struct tagged by unit/plane partitioning.',
  [ST+'common.rs',ST+'mod.rs',ST+'variant.rs',ST+'plane_partitioned.rs',ST+'unit_partitioned.rs'],
  'Per-kind validators/build/resource methods dispatch through StageVariant, but StageMatmulKind.expand_stage_matmul actually constructs all lhs/rhs/acc/out memory configs and validate_blueprint adds a common double-buffer constraint. Its all-methods-pure-two-arm-dispatch comment is therefore too broad. This is documentation drift in a real shared constructor, not a need to split more files. Unit/plane variants own different resource arithmetic.'),
 ('Output stage/global vector widths are unified by default stage construction','StageMatmulKind.expand_stage_matmul assigns out_smem_config.vector_size from vector_sizes.out.',
  [ST+'mod.rs',G+'write/plane.rs'],
  'This rules out treating the suspicious PlaneWriter wider-output gather branch as an ordinary path from this constructor: matching widths take the equal-width branch. Public/manual mixed-width use still has a distinct contract to inspect. Acc and out configs are initially identical values but represent reader versus clamped writer allocations; their separate lifetime/budget remains necessary.'),
 ('Register fragment ownership is explicit but initialization is delegated','init_a_fragment, init_b_fragments and init_accumulator allocate possibly uninitialized instruction-level tiles.',
  [ST+'common.rs'],
  'Documentation explicitly requires loading before execution. RHS partition buffering allocates one/two fragments independently of global A/B shared-memory stages. Accumulator is a partition tile with one tile perM*N partition cell, not automatically numerical zero in these helpers. The later load_partition_from_stage(None) implementation must initialize absent accumulators; no zero-init claim inferred here.'),
 ('Tile selector support hints differ from full validation','Cmma/Mma query exact hardware MmaConfig; Register/Interleaved/PlaneVec is_supported return true but validate impose dtype/layout/divisibility constraints.',
  [T+'cmma.rs',T+'mma.rs',T+'register.rs',T+'interleaved.rs',T+'plane_vec.rs',T+'common.rs',T+'variant.rs',T+'mod.rs'],
  'is_supported is an instruction-availability hint, not complete blueprint admission. Register and Interleaved share arithmetic type checks; PlaneVec additionally requires plane ops. Interleaved validate calls check_types_available with plane-op requirement false although execution may use plane primitives; actual tile execution remains unread. Cmma refuses swizzle and stage casting; Mma permits stage casts and device-aligned swizzle. No unsupported actual launch was exercised.'),
 ('Tile variant interfaces centralize dispatch while keeping separate arithmetic implementations','TileMatmul/Kind dispatch five per-variant contracts and generic allocation functions.',
  [T+'mod.rs',T+'variant.rs',T+'cmma.rs',T+'mma.rs',T+'register.rs',T+'interleaved.rs',T+'plane_vec.rs'],
  'Shared selector vocabulary does not mean one implementation of multiplication: each allocator maps to an independent generic tile backend. supported_sizes empty for software tile kinds is distinct from unsupported; valid software shapes are rule-derived. Precise numerical behavior, event ordering and memory layout reside in later root tile source. This is intentional modularity whose admission/behavior must remain consistent across all variants.'),
 ('Blueprints carry both logical bounds policy and kernel resource choices','BatchMatmulBlueprintBuilder derives M/N/K checks from stage extents and explicit stage_buffering.',
  [M+'definition/blueprint.rs',M+'definition/cube_mapping.rs',M+'definition/spec.rs'],
  'K-group buffering includes the full stage pair; a source regression test covers it but was not run. cube_launch_info rejects zero global partition dimensions before div_ceil; builder does not reject all degenerate stage values and USize-toU32 narrowing remains explicit. CubeMapping is actually re-exported/delegated to cubek-std with only matmul axis interpretation local. MatmulTypes carries global/stage/register sizes separately, a genuine typed ownership boundary.'),
 ('Tiling hierarchy centralizes counts but public fields can bypass builder constraints','TilingScheme computes parent/child products from tile, partition, stage and global partition sizes.',
  [M+'definition/tiling_scheme.rs',M+'cube_dim_resource.rs',M+'definition/blueprint.rs'],
  'Builder asserts stageK1 and checks only presence of required size values; public fields allow alternative/manual values. Count arithmetic isU32 and may overflow, CubeDimResource units-to-planes assumes nonzero plane_dim. These are configuration-domain followups, not proved reachable default crashes. adjust_dtypes can switch F32 accelerator compute toTF32 and Flex32 toF16 according to device support while retaining global types; declared storage precision is not complete compute precision.')]
